le_sha256" "c513381e386b074cae64cf800a2b6e4ed1a1ffbb396bbffa819854727f89417b"} {"question" "q-181600" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/assets/83ebd6f5d742a869b267a0cead4a9a94ae17fa534ca3e1cfddbb495c67390ecf.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,-x\\,{{field-2}}\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,2}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/state.json" "file_sha256" "c513381e386b074cae64cf800a2b6e4ed1a1ffbb396bbffa819854727f89417b"} {"question" "q-181600" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=-x$ and *below* the line $y=2.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>-x,\\,y<2.\n$$\n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\n-x<y<2.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the line $y=-x$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the corresponding inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\n-x\\le y<2\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-x\\le y<2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/state.json" "file_sha256" "c513381e386b074cae64cf800a2b6e4ed1a1ffbb396bbffa819854727f89417b"} {"question" "q-181600" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fd7aec7b89ddd4a554de8851428d4e55bf1012990a97ac62d7a942bcacf35152"} {"question" "q-181600" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/state.json" "file_sha256" "c513381e386b074cae64cf800a2b6e4ed1a1ffbb396bbffa819854727f89417b"} {"question" "q-181600" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "C"] ["math" "N"] ["math" "R"] ["math" "{C}^{2}"] ["math" "{R}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/state.json" "file_sha256" "c513381e386b074cae64cf800a2b6e4ed1a1ffbb396bbffa819854727f89417b"} {"question" "q-181600" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/state.json" "file_sha256" "c513381e386b074cae64cf800a2b6e4ed1a1ffbb396bbffa819854727f89417b"} {"question" "q-181600" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/state.json" "file_sha256" "c513381e386b074cae64cf800a2b6e4ed1a1ffbb396bbffa819854727f89417b"} {"question" "q-181600" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "<"] ["math" ">"] ["math" "\\ge "] ["math" "\\le "] ["math" "\\ne "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/state.json" "file_sha256" "c513381e386b074cae64cf800a2b6e4ed1a1ffbb396bbffa819854727f89417b"} {"question" "q-181600" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\le "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/state.json" "file_sha256" "c513381e386b074cae64cf800a2b6e4ed1a1ffbb396bbffa819854727f89417b"} {"question" "q-181600" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/state.json" "file_sha256" "c513381e386b074cae64cf800a2b6e4ed1a1ffbb396bbffa819854727f89417b"} {"question" "q-181600" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "<"] ["math" ">"] ["math" "\\ge "] ["math" "\\le "] ["math" "\\ne "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/state.json" "file_sha256" "c513381e386b074cae64cf800a2b6e4ed1a1ffbb396bbffa819854727f89417b"} {"question" "q-181600" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "<"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/state.json" "file_sha256" "c513381e386b074cae64cf800a2b6e4ed1a1ffbb396bbffa819854727f89417b"} {"question" "q-181694" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/assets/c670ed592fc32716596aae470911923627d1c6861a75a1c885659d09005e0a84.png)\n\nUse set builder notation to describe the shaded region given in the diagram above:\n\n${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n${x}^{2}\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n${y}^{2}$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$36$\n\n$}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/state.json" "file_sha256" "c513381e386b074cae64cf800a2b6e4ed1a1ffbb396bbffa819854727f89417b"} {"question" "q-181694" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the elliptical boundary of our region has horizontal radius $a=2$ and vertical radius $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can write as\n\n$$\n9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36.\n$$\n\nWe're interested in describing all points that lie *inside* the ellipse. So, let's pick any point inside the region, say, $(0,0).$ Substituting its coordinates into the equation of the boundary, we obtain\n\n$$\n9(0)^{2}+4(0)^{2}\\,<\\,36.\n$$\n\nAs a result, the points $P(x,y)$ in our region are any real numbers that satisfy the condition\n\n$$\n9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<36.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the curve $9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\n9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}\\le 36.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}\\le 36}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/state.json" "file_sha256" "c513381e386b074cae64cf800a2b6e4ed1a1ffbb396bbffa819854727f89417b"} {"question" "q-181694" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fd7aec7b89ddd4a554de8851428d4e55bf1012990a97ac62d7a942bcacf35152"} {"question" "q-181694" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/state.json" "file_sha256" "c513381e386b074cae64cf800a2b6e4ed1a1ffbb396bbffa819854727f89417b"} {"question" "q-181694" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/state.json" "file_sha256" "c513381e386b074cae64cf800a2b6e4ed1a1ffbb396bbffa819854727f89417b"} {"question" "q-181694" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/state.json" "file_sha256" "c513381e386b074cae64cf800a2b6e4ed1a1ffbb396bbffa819854727f89417b"} {"question" "q-181694" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/state.json" "file_sha256" "c513381e386b074cae64cf800a2b6e4ed1a1ffbb396bbffa819854727f89417b"} {"question" "q-181694" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/state.json" "file_sha256" "c513381e386b074cae64cf800a2b6e4ed1a1ffbb396bbffa819854727f89417b"} {"question" "q-181694" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\le"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/state.json" "file_sha256" "c513381e386b074cae64cf800a2b6e4ed1a1ffbb396bbffa819854727f89417b"} {"question" "q-181999" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/assets/c7f7b1dc9bf4da61b573345aaf92fe0d29ea00ef5558a9fca985d8af25fa0a03.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,y\\,{{field-2}}\\,2}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/state.json" "file_sha256" "c513381e386b074cae64cf800a2b6e4ed1a1ffbb396bbffa819854727f89417b"} {"question" "q-181999" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=2.$\n\nTherefore, a point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>2\n$$\n\nSince the boundary is *not* included in the set (the curve is *not* solid),  no further action must be taken, so we have\n\n$$\ny>2.\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y>2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/state.json" "file_sha256" "c513381e386b074cae64cf800a2b6e4ed1a1ffbb396bbffa819854727f89417b"} {"question" "q-181999" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fd7aec7b89ddd4a554de8851428d4e55bf1012990a97ac62d7a942bcacf35152"} {"question" "q-181999" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/state.json" "file_sha256" "c513381e386b074cae64cf800a2b6e4ed1a1ffbb396bbffa819854727f89417b"} {"questi